  "title": "The Emergency Address Has a Missing Piece",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "public safety/preparedness",
  "premise": "A preparedness class wants to practice describing a fictional location, but a landmark-only message leaves two possible buildings. A reviewed practice card adds the location details needed by the relevant local emergency system.",
  "hook": "Which of these two buildings does the message mean?",
  "visible_action": "Two matching landmark icons appear; fictional address and entrance-detail blocks resolve the ambiguity in a simulation.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Clear location information matters when communicating an emergency.",
  "gate": "Use simulation only, fake addresses, and local official instructions; never place a practice emergency call. Do not ask viewers to guess an emergency response or choose an action in a simulated emergency; any response content must come from reviewed official guidance.",
